{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on ae823d9a: A. archiveHostItem answers 'unbound' only when the row is present and its archive slot is not journal (a missing row stays as today unless you can show it is equally definite, then say so in the note); every other check stays forbidden and keeps the AR-1 backoff. The pass ends disabled with a durable unbound marker and one daily recheck; signal() leaves the marker alone outside the Directory, and a Directory commit that binds clears it. Not C. The review must state: (1) wake floor and requests per room per hour before and after for grow-demo (about 98/h to about 4/day), and for a busy lane like Room A that commits every minute (no per-commit pass); (2) who can receive the 'unbound' answer and that it reveals nothing to a caller who could not already read the row. Red per condition 4. Builder lane after PT-1.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}